{"type": "answer", "text": "The Moss documentation does not list a Rust SDK crate, so there is no crate name or 'cargo add' command to give you. The SDK Overview says Moss ships official SDKs for seven platforms: Python (pip install moss), JavaScript (npm install @moss-js/moss), Swift (iOS), Android, Elixir (Hex), Browser/WebAssembly (npm install @moss-dev/moss-web) and C (libmoss). Rust is not one of them. The C SDK page states that libmoss is distributed only as GitHub binary releases and is not published to crates.io. I would not guess a crate name. If you need Rust, the documented options are linking the C library (libmoss, shared library plus libmoss.h, needs glibc 2.28+ on Linux) or using the REST/HTTP API."}
